<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puno</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puno is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> on the western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-titicaca">Lake Titicaca</a>, at about 3,800 metres above sea level. Founded by the Spanish in 1668 near rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines, it is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puno-region">Puno Region</a>. It is known as a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aymara">Aymara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quechua">Quechua</a> culture and for the Candelaria festival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puno.jpg" alt="Puno" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tydence Davis from Las Vegas · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puno_cityscape.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
